INFO:agent.loop:\u26a1 Executing tool: 'knowledge_agent' with arguments: {"source_title": "Benchmark source synthesis: Ronin and Harmony Horizon thefts", "source_url": "SRC-001; SRC-002; SRC-003; SRC-004", "text": "Evidence returned by benchmark tools: SRC-001 (Elliptic, May 9 2023) states the FBI confirmed North Korea-backed Lazarus Group was behind the June 24 2022 Harmony Horizon Bridge hack, exploiting about $99.7m. Elliptic says its prior attribution relied on similarities with Lazarus blockchain laundering patterns; after the theft, transactions were programmatically structured through Tornado Cash. The article says the methods mirrored those used after the Ronin Bridge hack, and estimates more than $555m from the two hacks passed through Tornado Cash: over $468m from Ronin and $96m from Harmony. It further reports Horizon funds later structured into Railgun deposits, then sent to three crypto exchanges; Binance and Huobi announced blocking/seizing part. SRC-003 (Elliptic, Mar 29 2022, updated for Apr 14 sanctions) states Ronin announced theft of 173,600 ETH and 25.5m USDC, worth $540m at theft; OFAC sanctioned the thief's Ethereum address and listed its owner as Lazarus Group. Ronin's postmortem said five of nine validator private keys were obtained and evidence pointed to social engineering. Elliptic reports stolen USDC swapped for ETH via DEXs, then $16.7m ETH through three centralized exchanges, followed by Tornado Cash; $80.3m had gone through Tornado Cash and $9.7m sat in intermediary wallets as of the article date. It describes similarities to prior Lazarus attacks in victim location, believed social engineering, and laundering pattern. SRC-002 (Chainalysis, Sep 8 2022) states North Korea-linked groups, especially Lazarus Group, accounted for much DeFi theft; it describes Ronin laundering through more than 12,000 addresses. It outlines a five-stage pattern: stolen ETH to intermediary wallets; batches through Tornado Cash; ETH swapped for bitcoin; bitcoin mixed in batches; bitcoin deposited to crypto-to-fiat services. It also reports chain-hopping via bridges and swaps (Ethereum to BNB, ETH to USDD, then BitTorrent), and more than $30m seized, about 10% of total funds stolen. SRC-004 returned only a generic Elliptic resource page with no substantive case facts. No benchmark-returned evidence directly establishes APT38 as an alias or provides specific wallet addresses beyond the Ronin thief Ethereum address being sanctioned/listed as Lazarus Group; do not assert an APT38 identity link or invent addresses."}
